  "question": {
    "text": "Let $p$ and $q$ be any two logical statements and $\\mathrm{r}: \\mathrm{p} \\rightarrow(\\sim p \\vee q)$. If $r$ has a truth value $F$, then the truth values of $p$ and $q$ are respectively:",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "id": "8j8Cv",
      "text": "\n$\\mathrm{F}, \\mathrm{F}$\n",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "gqMja",
      "text": "\n$\\mathrm{T}, \\mathrm{T}$\n",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "7x6Fy",
      "text": "\n T, F\n",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": true
    },
    {
      "id": "EyYvV",
      "text": "\nF, T",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    }
  ],
  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "$p \\rightarrow(\\sim p \\vee q)$ has truth value $\\mathrm{F}$.\nIt means $p \\rightarrow(\\sim p \\vee q)$ is false.\nIt means $p$ is true and $\\sim p \\vee q$ is false.\n$\\Rightarrow p$ is true and both $\\sim p$ and $q$ are false.\n$\\Rightarrow p$ is true and $q$ is false.",
    "image": null
  },
